# core/reifies-audit - Is the reification bridge sound?
#
# Answers: which qualified relationships carry no triple term, and which carry one
# whose subject or object disagrees with arch:source / arch:target.
#
# Does NOT prove: that a sound bridge is a *correct* bridge. This checks the two
# halves of each relationship against each other, not against the source model. A
# relationship wrong in both halves agrees with itself and passes.
#
# Why both halves can disagree: the qualified resource states its endpoints twice,
# once as arch:source/arch:target and once inside the triple term. Nothing in RDF
# keeps them in step, and a hand-authored or hand-migrated bridge is exactly where
# they drift. A disagreeing bridge is worse than a missing one, because
# core/neighbours-reified and core/neighbours-qualified will then return different
# neighbours for the same element and both will look right.
#
# `missing-term` is not automatically a defect. The converters emit no bridge at
# all, so on converter output every relationship is reported and the finding is
# "this dataset has no bridge" - which core/discover-relationship-types tells you
# more cheaply. Run this on a dataset whose author added the bridge deliberately.
#
# EVERY BRANCH IS SELF-CONTAINED, and that is not stylistic. A UNION branch is a
# group graph pattern: variables bound in the enclosing group are not available
# where the branch's own FILTER is evaluated, and a FILTER comparing against an
# unbound variable is simply false. Hoisting the shared `arch:source`/`arch:target`
# patterns out of these branches made both disagreement checks match nothing, and
# they reported it as a clean bridge. Measured, both ways, against
# tests/test_reifies.py.
#
# Requires SPARQL 1.2; refused unless the profile declares capabilities.rdf_reifies.
#
# Parameters: LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT ?finding ?rel ?relType ?expected ?found
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    {
      ?rel a {{ROLE:relationship_class}} ;
           {{ROLE:rel_source}} ?source ;
           {{ROLE:rel_target}} ?target .
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?rel {{ROLE:reifies}} <<( ?any ?anyPredicate ?other )>> }
      BIND("missing-term" AS ?finding)
    }
    UNION
    {
      ?rel a {{ROLE:relationship_class}} ;
           {{ROLE:rel_source}} ?source ;
           {{ROLE:rel_target}} ?target ;
           {{ROLE:reifies}} <<( ?termSource ?predicate ?termTarget )>> .
      FILTER(?termSource != ?source)
      BIND("subject-disagrees" AS ?finding)
      BIND(?source AS ?expected)
      BIND(?termSource AS ?found)
    }
    UNION
    {
      ?rel a {{ROLE:relationship_class}} ;
           {{ROLE:rel_source}} ?source ;
           {{ROLE:rel_target}} ?target ;
           {{ROLE:reifies}} <<( ?termSource ?predicate ?termTarget )>> .
      FILTER(?termTarget != ?target)
      BIND("object-disagrees" AS ?finding)
      BIND(?target AS ?expected)
      BIND(?termTarget AS ?found)
    }
    OPTIONAL {
      ?rel a ?relType .
      FILTER(?relType != {{ROLE:relationship_class}} && ?relType != {{ROLE:concept_class}})
    }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?finding ?rel
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
